What was changed, for the make.fun markdown-render-speed-02 competition (output must stay identical to
marked.parse(markdown) with marked's default options):
- Specialized to the default options only (gfm on, breaks off, pedantic off, no extensions, hooks,
  custom renderers or walkTokens); the Tokenizer is folded into the Lexer and the Renderer/Parser into
  plain functions. The grammar regexes are still composed at load time by marked's own rules.
- Lists: first line found with indexOf/slice instead of split; tab expansion skipped on tab-free lines.
- Inline lexing: tokenizers are only tried when the current first character can start them; sources
  that can only produce one text token take a direct path; simpler but equivalent GFM text regexes are
  used when a source has no '@' (and no ':' or "www."); the emphasis mask skips replacements that
  cannot change anything; emphasis code-point handling no longer builds spread arrays.
- The emphasis mask and last-closer indexes are computed lazily, only when emphasis or
  strikethrough tokenizing actually needs them.
main.ts is a new driver written for the competition.
